          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मोर (mor) comes from mōra, a form CDIAL sets beside Sanskrit mayūra, \"peacock\" (CDIAL 9865). The source of the Sanskrit word is debated: Bloch traced it to Dravidian, Przyluski to Austroasiatic, and Bailey to an old Indo-Iranian colour word."
            }
          ]
        },
